{
  "title": "Gymnast's Wrist (Distal Radial Physeal Stress Syndrome)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6052/gymnasts-wrist-distal-radial-physeal-stress-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 8 2023",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Gymnast's wrist is a distal radius physeal injury most commonly due to overuse of the wrist primarily affecting young gymnasts.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with tenderness at the distal radius with radiographs showing widened distal radial growth plate with ill-defined borders.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment involves rest, NSAIDs and immobilization for 3-6 weeks. Rarely, in the case of premature physeal closure, surgical treatment is indicated.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "up to 25% of non-elite gymnasts",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "wrist undergoes supraphysiological loads due to use as a weight bearing joint.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "repetitive stress causes inflammation at growth plate of distal radius.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "microtrauma can lead to premature closure of distal radial physis resulting in secondary overgrowth of ulna.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "orthopaedic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**distal ulnar overgrowth**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**positive ulnar variance**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "wrist pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "usually radial sided",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may be chronic in nature",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "swelling may be present at wrist",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**tenderness to palpation at distal radius**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "decreased wrist flexion or extension may be present",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
